<Project>
  <!--
    Phase 263 — the release-candidate channel's version stamp.

    A release candidate is the lockstep <Version> from Directory.Build.props
    with a SemVer-2 prerelease label appended: `1.0.0` packs as
    `1.0.0-rc.1`. The label lives ONLY on the release tag (`v1.0.0-rc.1`);
    the tree keeps declaring the bare `1.0.0` it is a candidate for, so
    promotion is a new tag on a descendant commit, never a version edit.

    The `VerifyReleaseChannel` target (Build.fs) reads the tag, refuses one
    that does not name the declared version, and hands the two halves to
    every later step of the publish job as the environment variables
    TOOLUP_RELEASE_CORE (`1.0.0`) and TOOLUP_RELEASE_PRERELEASE (`rc.1`).
    MSBuild exposes an environment variable as a property of the same name,
    which is how they arrive here. Unset (every build that is not an RC
    publish), both conditions below are false and nothing changes.

    WHY A .targets FILE, NOT Directory.Build.props. A project's own
    <Version> override (the independently versioned `-alpha` packages, the
    Stripe line) is set in the .fsproj, which evaluates AFTER the props and
    BEFORE this file. Only here can the rule tell a lockstep project (its
    <Version> equals the core the tag names) from one that versions on its
    own.

    WHAT AN RC RUN PUBLISHES. Exactly the lockstep line, at the candidate
    version. A project on its own version line is made non-packable for the
    run: an RC must never be the run that first publishes a STABLE version
    of anything, and an independently versioned package has no candidate
    of its own to publish. No lockstep project references one of those
    projects, so no candidate package can declare a dependency on a
    package this run skipped.

    PackageVersion is set beside Version because the NuGet pack targets may
    already have defaulted it from the un-suffixed Version by the time this
    file is evaluated.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(TOOLUP_RELEASE_PRERELEASE)' != '' and '$(TOOLUP_RELEASE_CORE)' != '' and '$(Version)' == '$(TOOLUP_RELEASE_CORE)'">
    <Version>$(TOOLUP_RELEASE_CORE)-$(TOOLUP_RELEASE_PRERELEASE)</Version>
    <PackageVersion>$(TOOLUP_RELEASE_CORE)-$(TOOLUP_RELEASE_PRERELEASE)</PackageVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(TOOLUP_RELEASE_PRERELEASE)' != '' and '$(TOOLUP_RELEASE_CORE)' != '' and '$(Version)' != '$(TOOLUP_RELEASE_CORE)' and '$(Version)' != '$(TOOLUP_RELEASE_CORE)-$(TOOLUP_RELEASE_PRERELEASE)'">
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
